> I wasn't able to figure out how to pass those arguments via the summary() function

The ... argument just means you can use arguments of other functions that are called within summary(), or any generic function <http://web.mit.edu/~r/current/arch/i386_linux26/lib/R/library/methods/html/genericFunction-class.html#:~:text=Generic%20functions%20(objects%20from%20or,the%20function%20and%20its%20methods.>.

summary(fit, fit.measures = TRUE, pool.robust = TRUE, test = "D2")

The latter 2 arguments get passed to fitMeasures() inside summary(), when fit.measures = TRUE.

